# `thing instanceof Shape` walks no prototype chain. The shape words of a class and its subclasses are neighbors, so the two subclasses that are made here are one comparison with a bound. The word is loaded once. Behind the comparison the arm asks once more, now for the class with its subclasses, then reads the field by a plain load.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="measure" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[thing]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[word]] = Load(b@[[thing]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:AOTObject_shapeWord
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isSubclass]] = AboveEqual(b@[[word]], $-
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[isSubclass]], Terminal
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[shape]], Else:#[[other]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[shape]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #0
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isShape]] = AboveEqual(b@[[word]], $-
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isShape]], Terminal
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[area]], Else:Unlikely:#[[neither]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[area]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #[[shape]]
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[thing]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK: BB#[[other]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #0
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isLabel]] = Equal(b@[[word]], $-
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isLabel]], Terminal
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[size]], Else:Unlikely:#[[neither]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[size]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #[[other]]
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[thing]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# NONE-LABEL: name="measure" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: PrototypeLinks
# NONE-NOT: JSCell_structureID
# NONE-COUNT-1: AOTObject_shapeWord
# NONE-NOT: AOTObject_shapeWord
# NONE-NOT: PrototypeLinks
# NONE-NOT: JSCell_structureID
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# Some of the patchpoints are calls, and the moves around a call follow the calling convention, so the counts leave Windows out.
